  "id": "freecad_cw_sketch_007",
  "app": "freecad",
  "task": "Draw a regular pentagon with side length 5 centered at the origin with rotation angle 0. Use the zero-rotation orientation where one vertex lies on the positive X axis at (4.253254, 0), so the five vertices are at approximately (4.253254, 0), (1.314328, 4.045085), (-3.440955, 2.5), (-3.440955, -2.5), and (1.314328, -4.045085). Connect those vertices with exactly five straight outer edges to form one closed pentagon. Do not rotate the pentagon to make a flat top, flat bottom, or vertical side. Besides the five edges, the sketch must contain the pentagon's construction circumcircle (radius 4.253254, centred at the origin, marked as construction geometry), as FreeCAD's regular-polygon tool creates it, and no other geometry. Save the completed model to /home/user/Unnamed.FCStd.",
  "env": {
